<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       HARDWARE QUIRKS — DROIDWORKS_WIPE_SEVERITY_1 (packet B10).

       Owner ruling 7, verbatim: "Frequently also adds a permanent hardware
       quirk that cannot be reset but only accrete further." And the framework
       doc §1.3 on why a quirk is not simply a penalty: damaged brain parts stay
       in use — "rare and valuable still even quirky".

       THE POOL IS DEFINED BY THE MARKER, NOT BY A LIST IN C#. Every def below
       carries <modExtensions><li Class="...HardwareQuirkExtension" /></, and
       RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.DroidworksHardwareQuirks answers both
       "which traits can a wipe grant?" and "which traits must a wipe never
       strip?" off that one marker. A later packet adds a quirk with XML alone.

       🔑 THREE FIELDS DO THE WORK, and all three matter:
        * <commonality>0</commonality> — TraitDef.commonality, read by
          PawnGenerator's own RandomElementByWeight (PawnGenerator.cs:1570). At
          weight 0 a quirk can NEVER be rolled onto a randomly generated pawn,
          nor re-rolled by the memory wipe's own trait randomization. The only
          route in is DroidworksHardwareQuirks.TryGainRandomQuirk.
        * NO <exclusionTags> and NO <conflictingTraits>, on purpose. Quirks must
          ACCRETE — a droid wiped three times carries three of them — so nothing
          here may make two quirks mutually exclusive, and nothing may collide
          with the ordinary traits a wipe re-rolls.
        * NO <disabledWorkTags>/<disabledWorkTypes>. A quirk colours a droid; it
          never takes a work type away. Losing work capability permanently, on a
          roll, from a routine bench operation would be a different (and much
          crueller) design than ruling 7 describes.

       ⚠️ The stat numbers are FOUNDRY's own — no design doc sets any of them.
       They are deliberately small (5–15 %): the severity ruling 7 asks for
       lives in RSW_DW_RecentlyWiped's seven days, not in the permanent tail.
       Every StatDef named below was verified to exist in Core before use
       (Stats_Pawns_General/Social/WorkGeneral/Combat.xml).
  ======================================================================== -->

  <!-- Mechanical clumsiness that never quite calibrates out. -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_Quirk_ServoTwitch</defName>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.HardwareQuirkExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>servo twitch</label>
        <description>A wipe left this droid's actuator timing slightly out of true. Its manipulators overshoot and correct, over and over, at every task.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <commonality>0</commonality>
        <statFactors>
          <WorkSpeedGlobal>0.95</WorkSpeedGlobal>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

  <!-- The voice never came back quite right. -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_Quirk_VocoderGlitch</defName>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.HardwareQuirkExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>vocoder glitch</label>
        <description>Something in this droid's voice synthesiser was not restored cleanly. It clips, buzzes, and drops the ends of words. Nobody takes it quite seriously.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <commonality>0</commonality>
        <statFactors>
          <SocialImpact>0.85</SocialImpact>
          <NegotiationAbility>0.85</NegotiationAbility>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

  <!-- "It bumps into walls" made permanent, in miniature. -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_Quirk_GyroDrift</defName>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.HardwareQuirkExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>gyro drift</label>
        <description>This droid's balance package now runs a permanent bias. It walks a shade slower than it should and takes an extra beat to settle a weapon on target.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <commonality>0</commonality>
        <statFactors>
          <MoveSpeed>0.92</MoveSpeed>
          <AimingDelayFactor>1.10</AimingDelayFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

  <!-- The wipe took something out of the write path. -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_Quirk_MemoryHiccup</defName>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.HardwareQuirkExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>memory hiccup</label>
        <description>A bad sector this droid routes around and never repairs. New knowledge goes in slowly and comes back out with gaps in it.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <commonality>0</commonality>
        <statFactors>
          <GlobalLearningFactor>0.85</GlobalLearningFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

  <!-- "Rare and valuable still even quirky" (framework doc §1.3): the one
       quirk that is a trade rather than a tax. -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_Quirk_NarrowFixation</defName>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.HardwareQuirkExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>narrow fixation</label>
        <description>Whatever came back from the wipe came back narrower. This droid pursues a problem past the point anyone asked it to, and is very poor company while it does.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <commonality>0</commonality>
        <statFactors>
          <ResearchSpeed>1.10</ResearchSpeed>
          <SocialImpact>0.80</SocialImpact>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

</Defs>
